效果非常好。

1506
00:51:17.390 --> 00:51:20.410
I'm off to Australia and New Zealand in February.
二月份我要去澳大利亚和新西兰。

1507
00:51:20.730 --> 00:51:23.850
And then you did the whole East Coast, too, because I was texting with you and you were like –
然后你还跑了整个东海岸，因为我当时在给你发短信，你说——

1508
00:51:23.850 --> 00:51:24.890
Then I did the East CoaSt.
后来我去了东海岸。

1509
00:51:25.030 --> 00:51:26.090
I had a great tour there, too.
那里的巡演也很棒。

1510
00:51:26.090 --> 00:51:26.330
Yeah.
没错。

1511
00:51:26.530 --> 00:51:27.390
And the fans.
还有粉丝们。

1512
00:51:27.390 --> 00:51:31.650
And I want to thank all the Office fans for coming out and supporting my character and my music.
我想感谢所有《办公室》的粉丝们，感谢你们出来支持我的角色和我的音乐。

1513
00:51:31.670 --> 00:51:33.190
And it truly means a lot.
这对我来说意义重大。

1514
00:51:33.710 --> 00:51:36.010
I'm having my second childhood now doing this.
我现在做这些就像是在经历第二次童年。

1515
00:51:36.630 --> 00:51:38.610
And by the way, I have a surprise for you, ladies.
对了，女士们，我给你们带了个惊喜。

1516
00:51:38.730 --> 00:51:39.170
What is it?
是什么？

1517
00:51:39.230 --> 00:51:46.210
I brought – which I think may be the single, if there's going to be a single from my – I'm going to play you a little snippet, if you'd like.
我带来了——我觉得这可能会是主打歌，如果我的专辑里有主打歌的话——如果你们愿意，我可以给你们放一小段。

1518
00:51:46.390 --> 00:51:46.990
Yes, please.
好啊，请放吧。

1519
00:51:46.990 --> 00:51:48.290
Of the album.
专辑里的歌。

1520
00:51:48.510 --> 00:51:49.810
Can we do this in there?
我们可以在这里放吗？

1521
00:51:49.930 --> 00:51:51.130
Can I play it right now for you?
我现在能给你们放吗？

1522
00:51:51.510 --> 00:51:56.810
And you guys, before he plays the song, I just want to encourage you, if Creed is coming to a town near you,
还有各位，在他放歌之前，我想鼓励大家，如果克里德（Creed）要到你们附近的城市演出，

1523
00:51:56.810 --> 00:51:57.650
go see his show.
一定要去看他的演出。

1524
00:51:57.830 --> 00:51:58.770
It is fantastic.
非常精彩。

1525
00:51:59.190 --> 00:52:01.750
And apparently, he also makes fun of me during it.
而且显然，他在演出时还会拿我开涮。

1526
00:52:02.050 --> 00:52:03.310
Quite a bit, Angela, yes.
确实不少，安吉拉（Angela），没错。

1527
00:52:03.470 --> 00:52:09.730
And we are trying to figure out one of your locations where I can come on stage and give it to you right back.
我们正在研究你的演出地点，看我能不能上台去回敬你一下。

1528
00:52:09.870 --> 00:52:11.870
Where can people find the schedule?
大家去哪里可以查到演出日程？

1529
00:52:12.630 --> 00:52:13.450
Creedbratton.com.
Creedbratton.com.

1530
00:52:13.670 --> 00:52:14.390
We love you, Creed.
我们爱你，克里德。

1531
00:52:14.550 --> 00:52:15.410
All right, let's hear it.
好了，让我们听听看。

1532
00:52:15.450 --> 00:52:15.910
All right, here we go.
好的，开始了。

1533
00:52:16.210 --> 00:52:17.170
And the ride.
还有这段旅程。

1534
00:52:30.060 --> 00:52:34.220
Taught me how you taught me then
教会我你当时是如何教我的

1535
00:52:36.320 --> 00:52:41.020
How I could one day be your friend
我如何能有一天成为你的朋友

1536
00:52:42.840 --> 00:52:44.340
It's not so hot
没那么热

1537
00:52:46.310 --> 00:52:47.570
Just don't lie
只要别撒谎

1538
00:52:50.070 --> 00:52:50.870
Don't control
别去控制

1539
00:53:16.620 --> 00:53:18.600
All right, that's the song.
好了，歌就是这样。

1540
00:53:18.700 --> 00:53:19.320
There it is, gang.
就是这样，伙计们。

1541
00:53:19.480 --> 00:53:20.040
What do you think?
你们觉得怎么样？

1542
00:53:20.240 --> 00:53:21.720
Well, Angela's sobbing.
嗯，安吉拉在啜泣。

1543
00:53:21.900 --> 00:53:23.040
I just started crying.
我刚才突然就哭了。

1544
00:53:23.680 --> 00:53:28.080
The song is so beautiful, Creed, but also – and I totally am emotional, but –
这首歌太美了，克里德，但是——我完全被触动了，但是——

1545
00:53:28.740 --> 00:53:30.280
Oh, my God, it might be too emotional.
天哪，这可能太感人了。

1546
00:53:31.080 --> 00:53:32.060
Well, you know what?
好吧，你知道吗？

1547
00:53:32.160 --> 00:53:36.660
Do you ever have just like a wave hit you where you're like, you know you're in a special moment?
你有没有过那种感觉，就像一阵浪潮袭来，让你意识到自己正处于一个特别的时刻？

1548
00:53:36.660 --> 00:53:37.100
Yeah.
有。

1549
00:53:37.260 --> 00:53:37.580
Yes.
是的。

1550
00:53:37.680 --> 00:53:38.620
And it just hit me.
刚才那种感觉就袭向了我。

1551
00:53:38.720 --> 00:53:40.860
Well, I want to say with the two of you today.
好吧，我想说今天能和你们两位在一起。

1552
00:53:41.120 --> 00:53:41.200
Yeah.
没错。

1553
00:53:41.260 --> 00:53:42.620
I feel like we're in a special moment.
我觉得我们正处于一个特别的时刻。

1554
00:53:42.620 --> 00:53:46.220
It just felt really special and like something I'll always remember.
这种感觉真的很特别，就像我会永远铭记的事情一样。

1555
00:53:46.460 --> 00:53:50.320
And I'm facing my best friend who is now my boss lady business partner.
而我面对的是我最好的朋友，她现在是我的老板，也是我的商业伙伴。

1556
00:53:50.420 --> 00:53:54.140
And I'm so proud of us and this journey we've taken together.
我为我们感到骄傲，也为我们共同走过的这段旅程感到自豪。

1557
00:53:54.140 --> 00:53:56.820
And then I just love you, Creed.
还有，克里德，我真的很爱你。

1558
00:53:56.980 --> 00:53:58.120
Oh, I love you, sweetie.
噢，我也爱你，亲爱的。

1559
00:53:58.140 --> 00:53:58.500
I do.
我也是。

1560
00:53:58.520 --> 00:54:00.660
You're like, you know, family, family.
你就像，你知道的，家人，真正的家人。

1561
00:54:03.380 --> 00:54:07.480
Well, ladies and gentlemen, the last album I did, I had a song called More Than You Know.
各位女士先生，我做的上一张专辑里有一首歌叫《More Than You Know》。

1562
00:54:08.220 --> 00:54:12.480
And one of the first people I ever played it for was for you and Josh, you know, at your house.
我最早给听的人之一就是你和乔什，就在你们家里。

1563
00:54:12.600 --> 00:54:14.020
I came over and acoustically played it.
我过去用原声吉他弹奏了那首歌。

1564
00:54:14.160 --> 00:54:15.800
And she started crying.
然后她就开始哭了。

1565
00:54:15.820 --> 00:54:16.380
I started crying.
我也开始哭了。

1566
00:54:16.380 --> 00:54:17.440
I knew I had a winner then.
那时我就知道我写出了一首好歌。

1567
00:54:18.080 --> 00:54:25.940
Well, Creed, some of my favorite memories on the set were at lunchtime when you would play guitar and Ed would play banjo.
克里德，我在片场最美好的回忆之一就是午餐时间，你弹吉他，埃德弹班卓琴。

1568
00:54:26.300 --> 00:54:26.420
Yep.
没错。

1569
00:54:26.500 --> 00:54:27.920
Ed's trailer was next to mine.
埃德的拖车就在我隔壁。

1570
00:54:28.100 --> 00:54:31.400
You'd go in his trailer and the two of you would play through my lunch.
你们会去他的拖车里，整个午休时间都在演奏。

1571
00:54:31.580 --> 00:54:31.820
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1572
00:54:31.940 --> 00:54:32.380
And I just loved it.
我真的太喜欢了。

1573
00:54:32.380 --> 00:54:32.780
And you guys would call.
你们还会叫我。

1574
00:54:32.880 --> 00:54:35.140
You'd come over and stick your hand in and listen.
我会过去，探进头去听。

1575
00:54:35.140 --> 00:54:36.480
We'd come over and hang out.
我们会过去一起消磨时光。

1576
00:54:36.480 --> 00:54:43.420
For years, my alarm clock is banjo music because it would make me think of you guys.
多年来，我的闹钟一直是班卓琴音乐，因为那会让我想到你们。

1577
00:54:43.580 --> 00:54:50.080
And sometimes, especially when I was pregnant, if we had a little break, I might take a cat nap and I'd wake up to banjo music.
有时，特别是在我怀孕的时候，如果休息一会儿，我可能会小睡一下，然后被班卓琴声唤醒。

1578
00:54:50.280 --> 00:54:55.760
And it was like so pleasing that I made my alarm clock banjo because I thought, oh, maybe I won't wake up grumpy.
那感觉太美好了，所以我把闹钟设成了班卓琴声，我想，噢，也许这样我就不会起床时心情烦躁了。

1579
00:54:56.800 --> 00:54:57.880
Ed and I had so much fun.
我和埃德玩得非常开心。

1580
00:54:57.940 --> 00:54:59.140
He's a great banjo player.
他是个很棒的班卓琴手。

1581
00:54:59.220 --> 00:55:02.480
I haven't played with him in a long time because we're working all the time, but I would love to.
我们已经很久没一起演奏了，因为我们一直在忙工作，但我很想再和他一起弹。

1582
00:55:02.760 --> 00:55:03.140
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

1583
00:55:03.220 --> 00:55:04.660
You guys were great together.
你们俩在一起真的很棒。

1584
00:55:06.480 --> 00:55:09.520
Thank you so much for having me, my dear friends.
非常感谢你们邀请我，我亲爱的朋友们。

1585
00:55:09.700 --> 00:55:12.040
Creed, can we end with a final fan question?
克里德，我们能以最后一个粉丝提问来结束吗？

1586
00:55:12.140 --> 00:55:12.680
Yes, of course.
当然可以。

1587
00:55:12.860 --> 00:55:13.980
This is from Tim Blair.
这是蒂姆·布莱尔提的问题。

1588
00:55:15.000 --> 00:55:19.100
Tim asked, do you have a favorite Creed line from the whole show?
蒂姆问，在整部剧中，你最喜欢克里德的哪句台词？

1589
00:55:20.680 --> 00:55:21.900
Which one's Pam?
哪个是帕姆？

1590
00:55:24.920 --> 00:55:26.120
Which question, Pam?
什么问题，帕姆？

1591
00:55:26.280 --> 00:55:26.620
I could say.
我能说吗？

1592
00:55:27.680 --> 00:55:28.820
Gosh, I don't know.
天哪，我不知道。

1593
00:55:28.980 --> 00:55:34.360
It probably would be someone making soup or which one's Pam.
可能应该是关于有人在煮汤的那句，或者是“哪个是帕姆”。

1594
00:55:34.960 --> 00:55:35.880
Someone making soup.
有人在煮汤。

1595
00:55:35.880 --> 00:55:38.400
But I think, actually, I would have to be.
但我认为，其实，我不得不选那句。

1596
00:55:40.800 --> 00:55:47.160
In the 60s, I made love to many, many women, often outdoors in the rain and the mud.
在60年代，我和许多许多女人做过爱，经常是在户外，在雨中和泥地里。

1597
00:55:47.880 --> 00:55:49.660
It's possible a man slipped in.
有可能混进了一个男人。

1598
00:55:49.920 --> 00:55:51.060
There'd be no way of knowing.
根本没法知道。

1599
00:55:54.140 --> 00:56:01.600
From the booth, and that is how you end an episode, my friend.
来自导播间，我的朋友，这才是结束一集节目的方式。

1600
00:56:01.600 --> 00:56:02.280
Thank you, friend Amy.
谢谢你，艾米朋友。

1601
00:56:02.720 --> 00:56:03.400
Thank you, Creed.
谢谢你，克里德。

1602
00:56:04.950 --> 00:56:05.590
Thank you, everyone.
谢谢大家。

1603
00:56:06.010 --> 00:56:10.930
Please join us next week when we will be talking about the fight.
欢迎下周收听我们的节目，届时我们将讨论那场打斗。

1604
00:56:11.310 --> 00:56:11.890
The fight.
那场打斗。

1605
00:56:12.270 --> 00:56:12.490
Yeah.
没错。

1606
00:56:12.850 --> 00:56:13.730
We'll miss you, Creed.
我们会想你的，克里德。

1607
00:56:13.910 --> 00:56:15.110
You have to come back.
你一定要回来。

1608
00:56:15.210 --> 00:56:16.070
Well, I'd love to come back.
嗯，我很乐意回来。

1609
00:56:16.170 --> 00:56:16.430
Okay.
好的。

1610
00:56:18.750 --> 00:56:20.810
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1611
00:56:21.050 --> 00:56:24.550
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由 Earwolf、珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金赛制作。

1612
00:56:24.850 --> 00:56:26.570
Our producer is Cody Fisher.
我们的制片人是科迪·费舍。

1613
00:56:26.810 --> 00:56:28.630
Our sound engineer is Sam Kiefer.
我们的音响工程师是萨姆·基弗。

1614
00:56:28.850 --> 00:56:32.250
And our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿创作的《橡胶树》。

1615
00:56:32.250 --> 00:56:38.490
